  "query_preview": "..\nThis morning: Low stratus across the region will be pressed down\nto near the surface along higher elevations for most of the area\ncreating some fog starting around 3AM and last through Noon. \nDense fog will be possible in pockets for brief periods, but it \nis unknown as to exactly where and it will need to be reacted to \nlater this morning when it does occurs. This will lift back to low\nstratus in the afternoon hours. \n\nFriday PM through Sunday night: Large scale upper troughing \ncontinues across the western US the remainder of the week end. \nThe next system will bring another shot of arctic air from the \nnorth this weekend. A cut-off low is forecast to eject into the \nmain flow and will bring a weather system to the region beginning\nSaturday morning. This could generate isolated chances for snow \naround the edges of the CWA. However, the main impact will be the \nbelow normal temperatures with some wind chills post frontal \npassage. Wind chills this weekend are forecast to be in the teens\nto single digits during the morning hours. Wind behind the front \nmay bring speeds back up high enough to warrant a Lake Wind \nAdvisory that morning. but at this time it appears to be just \nbelow criteria and will need to be monitored for any up-tick.\n\nMonday to Wednesday: Zonal to northwest flow without any trough \nor ridge curvature will settle back in. Conditions will return to\nnear seasonal norms and remain relatively dry. \n\nWednesday night onward: Ensembles begin to massively disagree \nwith higher uncertainty in temperatures and heights Tuesday night \nonward. While temps do look near to slightly above normal the \nstate of curvature is all over the place blurring out the chances \nfor precipitation. Fully expect things to change here onward with \nfuture forecasts. \n\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\n- Deviations from NBM include a hourly visibility shake up from\n  NBM/GLAMP to a Majority Rules blend of remaining CAMs for TAFs\n  and possible Dense Fog.\n\n- Moderate confidence for light snow Friday through Monday night\n  (40%-60%).\n\n- Low confidence Wednesday night onward. Expect major changes to\n  forecast here.\n\nFINDLEY/GAH",
